{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_05a07e1178e8c5e7d9ded916316bfc503229a19baf78017ffda9dd363ecdfea1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3e463c6a0e5504a8d0c622245cf9529dab3d3bbbea188f36c48cfad4e607079e","slc_8d450918fff63b62c5cd402b21e9df039f937374a4bce53ace4661f2aabb567d"],"source_ids":["src_32790870da7a505c80a1053a62d8cf2f"],"text":"Repository development practice: the README's Development section lists cargo build, cargo test, cargo fmt, cargo clippy, and cargo build --features web, with docs/development.md as the full reference.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2a131aa5ca522dc99601d54d6a811461b6c9497152a456bdeada6cbcdf4018c0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6226c1b94573d37e9ab7488e91ed8c6d2ed3cb8855537d396a099c4757fac6ad","slc_9ffbd6266b5f7a361898976d108e6783d7e0dde7d24575ea37ab95bc8e138a0b","slc_fea50f899ee95cee77c34f28d08f01e1e43a65ea7d19761c5d3d98e56751febb"],"source_ids":["src_94422215930c52ccbbbbe48e8ae68797"],"text":"Skill sync propagates managed skills into agents' own directories with a never-overwrite rule: hand-edited copies are reported as conflicts and left untouched unless explicitly named in a `replace` list; automatic syncs never replace anything.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3c30ecddfee0b9a69b8e49f97128fd9594ff50b02f46c6d6d1942bdcc9975751","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_de8e2e862d4ad7e11e7243dc6f58851da9e1e1f4a12b1e1cf372cce334bc0aca"],"source_ids":["src_32790870da7a505c80a1053a62d8cf2f"],"text":"The product exposes TUI, web, CLI, and HTTP API surfaces, with status detection, notifications, persistent tmux sessions, git worktrees, multi-repo workspaces, and Docker/Podman/Apple Containers sandboxing.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_53e4b08c3ca90b122284cbbf1ff159126de02cb17b279e4880d5a17d22b48c19","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_aa839db097fca88e66e687cc79f2c6c58afeee6487daa7a06f8703e0d2c476e5"],"source_ids":["src_32790870da7a505c80a1053a62d8cf2f"],"text":"AoE is described as a session manager for AI coding agents on Linux and macOS, running agents in parallel across branches with persistent sessions and optional worktree or container isolation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6157dcd8aa7837420527ecf6abe3255d81d8ade69b6438cef458dca2553578f5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_168575363392edebe709b8309a13e778dc95f8523e91929303a4a80421566bbe"],"source_ids":["src_94422215930c52ccbbbbe48e8ae68797"],"text":"POST /api/sessions supports callback_url (fired on Waiting/Idle/Error transitions with loopback/private address rejection and fire-and-forget delivery) and idempotency_key so retries return the existing session instead of duplicating it.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_699d4bde830e954b2e3c8af759257034d25781422d9e591e222b18c6a0dc934f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a053e1e3746d4d6b6e07deb085be3f4cd68d9c9916adbd6d31df4cea3fcba3e5","slc_e8e17b3ff7c4fb5b66479ea1c98ec41185deb0ef9b5cfa8cc1dfdb6c81677c78","slc_f81ed616a21d238c560069c337e6ccc06e0f80dd8135482846d720c28a4b6c37"],"source_ids":["src_32790870da7a505c80a1053a62d8cf2f"],"text":"tmux is a required prerequisite and Docker is optional for sandboxing; the project is built with cargo, and native Windows is unsupported because AoE depends on tmux and POSIX process handling (WSL2 only).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7113bde0f45b0da92bbb4996fd1f6dbab00a8bb93db8c3aed13e2e5f26bd835f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5eb457bcbf5b51426e0b3df9d008e9e59a6d1c7d53bf61b9db7ccdd95d9015e5"],"source_ids":["src_94422215930c52ccbbbbe48e8ae68797"],"text":"`aoe serve` exposes an HTTP API so external orchestrators such as other agents, MCP tools, or CI scripts can drive sessions without attaching to a terminal; the web dashboard uses the same API plus internal routes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_808c47044ffa994cf6887b5978fb0bc576968d4b56b9190a6fd00e1889727a7a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_58b3e4660af7ab882f8b769fc7eff850a1e58ff8a6e715522fa16baad7a6feb0","slc_67f7fb89a837f5c7bf6560ac36db6c2858a889923fbc1f7fd237f6d159bb66e7"],"source_ids":["src_32790870da7a505c80a1053a62d8cf2f"],"text":"Each agent runs in its own tmux session, so sessions persist when the TUI closes, SSH disconnects, or the terminal crashes; sessions are only removed when explicitly deleted.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_85e23c8e780bebe07c64698b34364a98dd16ff6259c98d519d335c97b2e64bf6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4fad8e48afabd70904b04c0ca0570cad266d97ae300b06898d820a302537a73b","slc_6cf937e26dd8901e276d91ee4a07f03b35b347668730a1cd9d761f75cf2e67d4","slc_a09c03e822e8e72328a964f044a130e129b6979bc2c3c38d9a0f33662c0cea18"],"source_ids":["src_94422215930c52ccbbbbe48e8ae68797"],"text":"All HTTP endpoints require a token unless the server starts with --no-auth; the token is printed by `aoe serve` and accepted via bearer header, query parameter, or cookie. A --read-only mode blocks write endpoints with 403.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8a9aa4196aa788aebf4c267c42ab6ad1a199421c24621c2e6c14c32e4029c598","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5ef9ac842ad85dfe6a06066a864e0b98e8fc0586272b9dfda44a54c5d3a90ee4","slc_a534bd893a74262613aab5ad24c80c2309a89da3fb26eb2268fbb7422100037b","slc_bb4389cbc5d53aa11d82b6714b6e16c82856e1904368ad202efe6bea6689f5b0"],"source_ids":["src_a893430f24175333954a1aad35e73ea0"],"text":"Configuration is layered: global config, per-profile config, and repo-level .agent-of-empires/config.toml, with later layers overriding earlier ones only for explicitly set fields.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8b08a05cf45d14ccc99b06a37c22da5d09aa63970b0f2b0f29c7c5440b2ef0af","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8a75836693b2466a4fe448dd51054cbf39044ef0f9c7da37bab0ba3db2c7f810","slc_fe9a7c33185d3c6150597daad82f74f80a45d27a28c81f8fde3773bee8c95c28"],"source_ids":["src_32790870da7a505c80a1053a62d8cf2f"],"text":"The project is MIT licensed, with one file (src/tui/hyperlink.rs) containing code derived from the herdr project under Apache License 2.0.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a6811946eda9ac369ac397b5883cacc6cfaaa6cf2c204704cda8ef51fd81ae30","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5794a40081f4e606620c2bd37e7bb117b1aaacd8304018928b2caa0dac6e118a","slc_f3fa49e5ea6f60c1c6ed3b53273531fa5f3e979575c663eae44d4ddff6723a17"],"source_ids":["src_94422215930c52ccbbbbe48e8ae68797"],"text":"Session status values are PascalCase on the wire (Starting, Running, Waiting, Idle, Error, Stopped, Unknown, Deleting, Creating), differing from the lowercase form used by the CLI and status-hook env vars.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ad41e2d9e7e91d51623c3539bec180871338261fee67b92bd0280621cb5c1f93","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bdda01bdc98eab35351b6f8d10d0bce70ef03765b6658e8deb7af6881241d14f","slc_d6819a59c2d71d113a1be8d341dc448e0aa79fc7a635b510334755cbb730d8cb"],"source_ids":["src_94422215930c52ccbbbbe48e8ae68797"],"text":"GET /api/sessions/{id}/output returns a tmux pane snapshot with configurable trailing-line count (clamped 1..=2000) and text or ansi format, and works under read-only mode.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cd49d6f3f5ff4ea1ea8c43a96af2cc9d4596ccc1b141ad622b664bccef1825fd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5a66eb056cfb26e6f203ba6d8fddcb9552d5b602c31c3501fbe76c04d4906ee4","slc_c8ae6aa33faf51e9cfe2f7c1e37aa1b19544cf7bc31d28e1571f7e3d63824f19"],"source_ids":["src_94422215930c52ccbbbbe48e8ae68797"],"text":"The send and output endpoints together form a documented primitive for driving an AoE session as a controlled subagent: send a prompt, poll output until stable or status returns to Idle, then capture the reply.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e11b39d8b2fbcd856ced9908a2d0d741b702180dd5852ed46954256e297b99e0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"agent-of-empires/agent-of-empires@bdf21c256673 snapshot 22bc1106b960b799","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3bb3c2d3246d035cdbf50893f05865b3e92ec3b83cb40cb37161e7988f4920e8","slc_716d8c24acde9dd9e0309ad19c832c2b50871d9c149e63cf00fd8ae6fbdd4bac"],"source_ids":["src_94422215930c52ccbbbbe48e8ae68797"],"text":"AoE discovers Agent Skills packages from a managed store and user-level agent directories (e.g. ~/.claude/skills, ~/.agents/skills, ~/.gemini/skills); a skill is a directory with a SKILL.md containing name and description frontmatter.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:30:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8c5a13328d254ea4884ad31c522b4a9a"}
